-- The root (MMS-521): the one place to ask what the law gives. For each pay
-- item it imports every instrument that speaks to it, gathers what each
-- says for a case (its claim, stated in the shared vocabulary), and asks
-- precedence (l4/lib/precedence.l4, encoded once) which one governs and by
-- which rule. The calculator, the contradictions page and any other query
-- ask this module, and an instrument's claim is never the answer by itself.
--
-- Where two or more instruments give different answers for an item and a
-- case, that is a contradiction (`the contradictions on` item case). This
-- module answers any case; what was checked lives beside it, in its tests
-- (l4/tests/root-tests.l4): the grid of cases, the contradictions found
-- over it, the resolution of each — which instrument governs and by which
-- rule, which precedence must agree with — and the gate that no
-- contradiction is left unresolved (the client, 2026-10-22: the root holds
-- no questions; they are in the test file).
--
-- Nothing here is about one item: an item is a `pay item` of the shared
-- vocabulary, and every function takes it.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `takanon-root`
IMPORT `agreements-root`
IMPORT `circulars-root`

§ `השורש — מקור אחד לשאלה מה הדין נותן`

§§ `המסמכים`

-- The instruments, and what each says, are registered in the collections'
-- roots: l4/lib/takanon-root.l4, l4/lib/agreements-root.l4 and
-- l4/lib/circulars-root.l4. This module asks them, in that order.

§§ `השאלה`

-- Every instrument that speaks to an item, and what it says for a case:
-- the takanon's, the agreements' and the circulars' claims.
GIVEN i IS A `pay item`, c IS A `teaching case`
GIVETH A LIST OF `claim`
DECIDE `the claims on` i c IS
    concat (LIST `the takanon's claims on` i c,
                 `the agreements' claims on` i c,
                 `the circulars' claims on` i c)

GIVEN i IS A `pay item`, c IS A `teaching case`
GIVETH A MAYBE `ruling`
DECIDE `the ruling on the item` i c IS
    `the ruling on` (`the claims on` i c) (c's `employer`) (`the date the takanon's provision on it was last amended` i)

@export What a teaching employee is owed for a pay item in a salary month, after precedence between every instrument that speaks to it; nothing where no instrument speaks
GIVEN i IS A `pay item` @desc the pay item asked about
      c IS A `teaching case` @desc the salary month, the employer, the division, the union, and the salary components the item needs
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the answer that governs` i c IS
    CONSIDER `the ruling on the item` i c
    WHEN JUST r THEN JUST (r's `the answer`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- The items asked about, each checked over the cases below.
`the items` MEANS
    LIST `the 2008 public-sector supplement`,
         `the pedagogical coordinator's allowance rate`,
         `the mentor's allowance rate`,
         `the junior-division head's allowance`,
         `the role allowances counted`

§§ `סתירות`

@desc A contradiction: for an item and a case, the instruments that speak give two or more answers.
DECLARE `contradiction` HAS
    `item`     IS A `pay item`
    `sources`  IS A LIST OF STRING @desc the modules of every instrument that speaks, in the root's order
    `answers`  IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc each answer given, once
    `the ruling` IS A `ruling`

GIVEN item IS A `pay item`
      claims IS A LIST OF `claim`
      r IS A MAYBE `ruling`
GIVETH A LIST OF `contradiction`
DECIDE `the contradiction in` item claims r IS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
    WHEN JUST governing THEN
        IF count (nub (map (GIVEN c YIELD c's `answer`) claims)) AT LEAST 2
        THEN LIST (`contradiction` WITH
                      `item`    IS item
                      `sources` IS map (GIVEN c YIELD c's `by`'s `module`) claims
                      `answers` IS nub (map (GIVEN c YIELD c's `answer`) claims)
                      `the ruling` IS governing)
        ELSE EMPTY

GIVEN i IS A `pay item`, c IS A `teaching case`
GIVETH A LIST OF `contradiction`
DECIDE `the contradictions on` i c IS
    `the contradiction in` i (`the claims on` i c) (`the ruling on the item` i c)
